  "id": "0445acd6-ab69-59ca-aa71-09cb6cd0766c",
  "slug": "fresh-cherry-pie",
  "name": "Fresh Cherry Pie",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "Fresh cherries and a hint of vanilla poured into a homemade crust make this classic cherry pie the perfect dessert for any summer gathering.",
  "cuisine": "U.S. American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Whisk flour and salt together in a bowl. Cut in butter with 2 knives or pastry blender until the mixture resembles coarse crumbs. Add cold water, 1 tablespoon at a time, tossing with a fork, until flour mixture is moistened. Do not add more water than you need: when you squeeze a handful of the moistened pastry mixture, it should form a ball."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Divide the dough in half and shape into balls. Wrap in plastic wrap and refrigerate, at least 1 hour or up to 3 days."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Preheat oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C)."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Meanwhile, mix cherries, sugar, and tapioca flour together in a saucepan; let sit until the sugar draws out the cherries' juices, about 10 minutes. Heat the cherry mixture over medium heat until the juices begin to thicken and run clear, about 5 minutes. Remove from heat; mix in butter and vanilla extract. Let sit until filling has cooled to lukewarm, 5 to 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Roll out half the pastry to fit a 9-inch pie plate. Place bottom crust in pie plate. Spoon filling into crust using a slotted spoon to drain excess syrup; dot with butter. Cut leftover dough into strips with a sharp paring knife or pastry wheel. Lay strips on top of the pie, pressing to seal the edges."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until crust is a golden brown, 40 to 50 minutes."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 40,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 20,
  "rest_time_minutes": null,
